    "created_at": "2018-11-21T20:33:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-11-21T20:33:19Z",
    "body": "> Gecko's stable state handling is based on the pre-stable-state-during-microtask model \r\n\r\nYes.  My point is, so is everyone else's as far as I can tell.  So why do we think it's web-compatible to change that model?",
