    "updated_at": "2018-11-21T21:53:19Z",
    "body": "From digging, the *\"Top: Await a stable state.\"* language was added in https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/41f85891ff9df346146e300ff59a85808e21524d, predating the microtask/stable state merge.\r\n\r\nAt that point the definition used to be: *\"When the user agent is to provide a stable state, if any asynchronously-running algorithms are awaiting a stable state, then the user agent must run their synchronous section and then resume running their asynchronous algorithm (if appropriate).\"*\r\n\r\nIf we're looking for original intent. I have no strong opinion on the matter.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
